==API Response==
autonumber 2.1
group __init__ constructor function
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: The constructor function is called whenever an instance foe calss APIResponse is created
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: This constructor gets data, errors as optional list of error ,integer code as optional  and string message as optional as inbound parameters
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: INbound data, errors, code is assigned for respective object's  attributes
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: A uuid is created, formatted into string data type amd stored in attribute request_id 

    alt if message not None
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Attribute message of the object is assigned with inbound message
    else if no errors & no message
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Attribute message of the object is assigned with custom message as Success
    else if length of errors is 1
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Attribute message of the object is assigned with error message in list error
    end
end group

group to_dict() function
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: This function is called when an APIResponse object needs to converted into dictionary format
    alt if data is not empty
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign the APIResponse objects data in key "data"
    else if data is empty
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign data as none  in key "data"
    end
    alt if errors is not empty
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Iterate over the errors and convert into dictonary using to_dict function and store in key "errors"
    else if errors in empty
        APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign errors as empty list  in key "data"
    end
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign inbound objects code in key "Status_code"
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign inbound objects request_id in key "request_id"
    APIResponse -> APIResponse: Assign inbound objects message in key "messages"
end group

==Custom Exception==
autonumber 2.2
group __init__ constructor function
    CustomException -> CustomException: This constructor function is called when object is created for class CustomException
    CustomException -> CustomException: The constructoe gets string message, string code, integer status and List of errors as Optional as inbpound parameter
    CustomException -> CustomException: Inbound message is assigned for object's message attribute
    CustomException -> CustomException: Attribute code, status_code is assigned with inbound code and status_code
    CustomException -> CustomException:  A uuid is created, formatted into string data type amd stored in attribute request_id 
    CustomException -> CustomException: Object's error attribute is assigned eith inbound errors
end group
group to_api_response function
    CustomException -> CustomException: Returns the instance of class APIResponse with no data, errors and code as attributes for instance creation 
    APIResponse <- CustomException
end group

